# API guide

> Read-only JSON over the curated profile records. No key, no account, no
> authentication. `<%= SiteMetadata.origin %>/openapi.json` is the normative
> description; this page is the human-readable guide.

## Base URL

```
<%= SiteMetadata.origin %>/api/v1
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/v1/profile` | Identity, headline, region, working mode, and profile links. |
| GET | `/api/v1/experience` | Roles, organizations, dates, and descriptions. |
| GET | `/api/v1/case-studies` | Selected work with technologies and outcomes. |
| GET | `/api/v1/projects` | Open-source projects with repository URLs. |
| GET | `/api/v1/skills` | Competency groups and their items. |
| GET | `/api/v1/education` | Credentials and institutions. |
| GET | `/api/v1/metrics` | Impact figures with their context. |
| GET | `/api/v1/records` | Every published record, all types. |

Every endpoint accepts `?locale=pt-BR` and defaults to `en`.

## Errors

Errors are JSON, never HTML:

```json
{ "error": { "code": "not_found", "message": "No such record type: widgets" } }
```

A rejected parameter returns `422` with the same shape and a `details` array.

## Rate limits and caching

One request per second is plenty. Responses carry a weak `ETag` and
`Cache-Control: public, max-age=300`; send `If-None-Match` to get a `304`.

## Contact

`<%= SiteMetadata.origin %>/llms.txt` names the maintainer and the profile links.
